From: Armada OS <armada@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wsa881x: select DRE PA gain when the COMP port is active

The WCD934x companders (COMP7/8) compress the RX signal and stream
per-sample gain (DRE) data to the WSA881x over the soundwire COMP port,
where the PA is meant to expand it back.  The driver unconditionally
forces PA_GAIN_SEL_REG, so with companders enabled (the vendor default
on the AYN Odin: COMP7/8 + SpkrLeft/Right COMP Switch all on) the amp
plays the compressed signal at static gain and output is severely
attenuated.  Select DRE gain when the COMP port is prepared, matching
the downstream driver's behaviour.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa881x.c	2026-07-22 09:09:01.780899916 -0500
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa881x.c	2026-07-22 09:09:11.117284828 -0500
@@ -929,9 +929,22 @@
 		regmap_multi_reg_write(wsa881x->regmap, wsa881x_pre_pmu_pa_2_0,
 				       ARRAY_SIZE(wsa881x_pre_pmu_pa_2_0));
 
-		snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, WSA881X_SPKR_DRV_GAIN,
-					      WSA881X_PA_GAIN_SEL_MASK,
-					      WSA881X_PA_GAIN_SEL_REG);
+		/*
+		 * With the COMP port active the codec compander streams
+		 * dynamic gain data to the PA (DRE); the PA must then take
+		 * its gain from that data, not the static gain register,
+		 * or playback is stuck at the compressed level.
+		 */
+		if (wsa881x->port_prepared[WSA881X_PORT_COMP])
+			snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp,
+						      WSA881X_SPKR_DRV_GAIN,
+						      WSA881X_PA_GAIN_SEL_MASK,
+						      WSA881X_PA_GAIN_SEL_DRE);
+		else
+			snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp,
+						      WSA881X_SPKR_DRV_GAIN,
+						      WSA881X_PA_GAIN_SEL_MASK,
+						      WSA881X_PA_GAIN_SEL_REG);
 		break;
 	case SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU:
 		if (wsa881x->port_prepared[WSA881X_PORT_VISENSE]) {
